NNOOTTEESS
       A new thread inherits a copy of its creator’s signal mask.

       The glibc pptthhrreeaadd__ssiiggmmaasskk() function silently ignores attempts to block
       the two real‐time signals that are used internally by the NPTL
       threading implementation.  See nnppttll(7) for details.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
       The program below blocks some signals in the main thread, and then
       creates a dedicated thread to fetch those signals via ssiiggwwaaiitt(3).  The
       following shell session demonstrates its use:

           $ ..//aa..oouutt &&
           [1] 5423
           $ kkiillll --QQUUIITT %%11
           Signal handling thread got signal 3
           $ kkiillll --UUSSRR11 %%11
           Signal handling thread got signal 10
           $ kkiillll --TTEERRMM %%11
           [1]+  Terminated              ./a.out

